 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Material/Color Changes:** Polygonizers generating meshes from CSG level sets do not inherently consider material properties. This can lead to drastic color changes between vertices at CSG boundaries if materials are not treated as surface boundaries (inside/outside changes) [S5, unofficial].
-*   **Signed Distance Bound Accuracy:** Intersection and Difference operations do not preserve the exact signed distance property. The resulting field is a bound, which may cause sphere tracing to step conservatively compared to an exact SDF, though it remains valid for rendering [S2].
